{"task_id": "HumanEval/31", "solution": "from math import isqrt\n\n\ndef is_prime(n):\n    \"\"\"Return true if a given number is prime, and false otherwise.\n    >>> is_prime(6)\n    False\n    >>> is_prime(101)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(11)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(13441)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(61)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(4)\n    False\n    >>> is_prime(1)\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n == 2:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0:  # Other even numbers are not prime\n        return False\n\n    # Check for odd divisors from 3 up to the square root of n\n    # isqrt(n) returns floor(sqrt(n))\n    for i in range(3, isqrt(n) + 1, 2):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True"}
